DEFECT-01 store.verify_chain raised TypeError instead of E_CHAIN_BROKEN when a tampered ledger row changed storage class BLOB->TEXT (found by test_hash_chain_detects_tamper_reorder_truncate); fixed: non-BLOB body is reported as E_CHAIN_BROKEN
DEFECT-02 authz.decide recursed into the separation-of-duties check for the second approver, so every two-person approval was denied (E_AUTHZ_SOD_APPROVER) — found by test_separation_of_duties; fixed with an approver-mode evaluation that checks the approver's own permission without demanding a third person
DEFECT-03 an exact network retry of already-accepted evidence was rejected with E_ATT_NONCE_UNKNOWN because the single-use attestation nonce was consumed before the idempotency check — found by test_exact_retry_idempotent_conflicting_resubmission_quarantines; fixed: an authenticated, signature-verified submission whose producer/event id and payload digest match the ledger returns 'duplicate' before nonce consumption
DEFECT-04 POST /v1/certify validated the request body before authenticating, so an unauthenticated caller received shape-validation detail (400) instead of 401 — found by test_contract_routes_and_error_codes; fixed with CertificationService.certify_request (authenticate -> validate -> authorize)
DEFECT-05 conflict resolution 'both-invalid' and bulk revocation re-used the caller's single-use token for every internal revoke, so the second internal call failed with E_AUTH_REPLAY and the workflow half-applied — found by test_both_invalid_quarantines_evidence; fixed by an internal _revoke() path taking the already-authenticated principal
